[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: VeloSim bounded RTL requirements
UID: VS-SRS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-BLOCK-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Selected blocking word assignment
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall apply supported bit, fixed-part and indexed-part blocking writes to writable 1..128-bit words, preserving untouched bits and making the result visible to later statements in the same process. Unknown indices shall suppress writes; partially out-of-range selections shall modify only in-range bits. Known selected-write bases above INT32_MAX shall raise the existing qualified-range error.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: RtlDesign.Statement, WordWrite and ProcessStatement; runtime deposit_indexed; UHDM expr lowering of logic_var declarations behind selections. Verification: RequirementIteration001..080 and 161..168, the minimized UhdmLogicVariableBlockingSelectionMatchesIcarus regression, plus seeded robustness tests. Evidence: ``artifacts/requirements-200/test-*.log`` and per-case manifest.json/commands.log. Acceptance status and final regression/coverage gates are recorded in docs/requirements-200.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/VeloSim.Core/RtlDesign.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: native/rtl/runtime.h
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: native/uhdm/rtl.cpp
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlRequirements200Tests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-BLOCK-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Concatenated blocking destinations
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall support concatenated blocking assignments to distinct writable signal words or supported selections with a combined width of at most 128 bits. It shall sample the RHS and all target index expressions before publishing any destination's local blocking result.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: RtlDesign.Statement and TargetLeaves. Verification: RequirementIteration081..100 and 169..172. Case 100 independently checks that a destination used as another destination's index retains its pre-assignment value for that index. Evidence: artifacts/requirements-200/ and docs/requirements-200.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/VeloSim.Core/RtlDesign.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlRequirements200Tests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-BLOCK-003
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Fixed-memory blocking assignment
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall support blocking writes to whole elements of supported fixed one-dimensional four-state memories. Later statements in the same process shall read the updated element. Invalid or unknown memory indices shall retain the existing unknown-read/ignored-write policy and other elements shall persist.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: RtlDesign.Statement, MemoryIndex, ProcessStatement and runtime read/write. Verification: RequirementIteration101..120 and 173..176, with nonzero bounds, persistence and unknown/out-of-range indices. Selected memory-element writes, two-state memories and memory elements inside concatenation targets are outside this contract. Evidence: artifacts/requirements-200/.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/VeloSim.Core/RtlDesign.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlRequirements200Tests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-BLOCK-004
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Blocking ownership and race rejection
STATEMENT: >>>
The validator shall reject mixed blocking/nonblocking writes to the same parent word or whole memory and shall reject blocking storage read by another process or continuous logic. Ownership and isolation shall hold independently of declaration order and target selection shape. Memory dependencies shall include the memory identity and its index expressions.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: RtlDesign.References, TargetOwner and ValidateBlockingIsolation. Verification: RequirementIteration121..160 and reproducible malformed-input/property tests. Mutation probes shall remove relevant guards and establish that focused tests detect the changed behavior. Evidence and limitations: docs/requirements-200.md and artifacts/requirements-200/.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/VeloSim.Core/RtlDesign.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlRequirements200Tests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-BLOCK-005
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Two-state blocking storage
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall coerce X/Z bits to zero at writes to two-state signal storage, including selected blocking writes. Later same-process reads shall observe the coerced result; untouched bits shall preserve their two-state value.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Implementation: RtlDesign.StoreWord, WordWrite and Statement. Verification: RequirementIteration181..200, existing signed two-state integration tests and final coverage. Evidence: artifacts/requirements-200/ and docs/requirements-200.md.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: src/VeloSim.Core/RtlDesign.cs
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/VeloSim.Tests/RtlRequirements200Tests.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-QUAL-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Reproducible qualification evidence
STATEMENT: >>>
Qualification shall retain stable case IDs, implementation/input/executable fingerprints, command results, reproducible randomized seeds, mutation outcomes and malformed-input results. Mutation acceptance shall require a passing control and distinguish semantic assertion failures from build, timeout and infrastructure failures. Coverage reports shall distinguish line and branch measurements, measured object scope and tooling limitations. Coverage shall not substitute for behavioral comparisons.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Verification ledger: docs/requirements-200.md; native execution evidence: ``artifacts/requirements-200/native/<run>/NNN/manifest.json``, status.json and commands.log. Same-source HDL evidence uses unique ``rtl-indexed-requirements-NNN-*`` directories under checkout artifacts or the configured VELOSIM_RTL_EVIDENCE_ROOT. Final coverage, mirror and source/binary evidence paths are recorded in the ledger after completion. AI reviews occur at 15-case boundaries and before the final commit. The full suite has a bounded 240-minute budget; individual fixture tool deadlines remain shorter. CI allows packaging headroom and measures the Linux test run once through coverage.
<<<
