UID: VS-RTL-TYPE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Composite and broader scalar types
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support structures, unions, enums and additional scalar integer types.
COMMENT: Open backlog; supported signed/unsigned logic/bit words remain bounded to 128 bits.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-ARRAY-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: General array and container operations
STATEMENT: The simulator shall support multidimensional, queue, dynamic and associative array operations.
COMMENT: Open backlog; this batch only extends blocking writes to whole elements of existing fixed one-dimensional memories.

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-COMB-002
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Acyclic fully assigned combinational blocks
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall settle bounded always_comb blocks together with continuous assignments in dependency order before sequential sampling and after the nonblocking commit. Within each block it shall preserve blocking statement order and procedural four-state conditions. Assignments may concatenate distinct whole-word parents up to 128 combined bits. Every whole-word destination shall have one owner and be assigned on every path before it is read. Feedback, read-before-write, latches, combinational memory writes, selected combinational writes and event-input-dependent combinational logic shall be rejected.
<<<
COMMENT: >>>
Qualified by batch combinational-subroutines-200, 831 executed full-regression passes and coverage gate 20261025-042139-8795316: RtlCombinational200Tests cases 001..040 and CombinationalRepeatSettlesBeforeEdge; external SDK first evaluation, no-edge input changes, repeated eval, pre-edge sampling and post-commit settling; RtlCombinationalRobustnessTests including aggregate budget rejection. The clockless extension is specified by VS-RTL-CLOCKLESS-001. VS-RTL-COMB-001 remains the broader backlog.
<<<
