- TYPE: File
  VALUE: native/rtl/timed_events.h
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tests/native/container_event_tests.cpp
- TYPE: File
  VALUE: tools/ContainerEventMutationProbe.cs

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-DYNAMIC-ARRAY-001
STATUS: Active
TITLE: Bounded dynamic array allocation through HDL
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall lower typed module-scope one-dimensional dynamic arrays into owning native storage and execute blocking new[count], self-preserving new[count](same_array), indexed reads/writes, zero-argument size and delete. Elements shall preserve supported word width, signedness and two/four-state defaults. Counts shall be sampled once and known, nonnegative and at most 256. Dynamic storage shall start empty, preserve the common prefix only for self-preserving allocation, initialize new cells and reject conflicting process ownership. SDK evaluation failure shall restore storage and edge history. Queue/associative methods, cross-array copies and general timed scheduling remain outside this bounded contract.
<<<
COMMENT: User-requested bounded slice:21 focused tests pass against original HDL/Icarus, independent traces, standalone and SDK models, including failure recovery after a truncating allocation. Selected regression, malformed-input properties, native semantic mutations, Stryker.NET and coverage evidence are documented in docs/dynamic-arrays.md. The Icarus two-state invalid-read limitation is recorded separately from native default-value checks.
