[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-QUEUE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded HDL queue lifetimes
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall lower module-scope one-dimensional integral queues into initially empty owning storage and support push_front, push_back, pop_front, pop_back, size, whole or indexed delete, and blocking indexed access. A write at the current size shall append. Empty pops and invalid reads shall return the declared element default. Unknown or invalid deletion indices and farther out-of-range writes shall leave storage unchanged. A 256-cell resource limit shall reject overflow before the failing operation changes storage. Pops shall be explicit ordered statements with discarded results or blocking whole-word destinations. Mutating queues shall be isolated from other processes and combinational readers. SDK evaluation failure shall restore queue contents, outputs and edge history. Bounded queue declarations, nested/aggregate queues, queue ports, nested side-effect expressions and general timed scheduling are outside this slice.
<<<
COMMENT: Implemented bounded slice under focused qualification only, as requested by the user. Broad regression acceptance has not been rerun; retain Draft. See docs/queues.md and the current handoff for actual scoped verification evidence.
