[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-ASSOCIATIVE-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Bounded integral associative arrays
STATEMENT: >>>
The simulator shall lower module-scope associative arrays with integral keys and packed elements of 1 through 256 bits into owning ordered native storage. At most 256 populated entries shall be supported, while updates to existing entries remain permitted at capacity. Missing reads shall return the element default without inserting cells. Unknown keys shall not create or delete entries. The simulator shall support num, exists, keyed/all deletion and first/last/next/prev traversal in numeric key order, preserving the index on failed traversal. SDK evaluation failure shall restore associative state.
<<<
COMMENT: Inferred bounded acceptance contract for the user-requested associative-array work. Implementation and qualification remain in progress; no verified closure. String/wildcard keys, nested associative arrays and aggregate elements remain outside this slice. docs/associative-arrays.md records current evidence and observed Verilator 5.020 limitations. General array support remains Draft under VS-RTL-ARRAY-001.
