[REQUIREMENT]
UID: VS-RTL-SCHEDULER-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Executing bounded active inactive and NBA kernel
STATEMENT: >>>
The explicit-time kernel shall execute active work, zero-delay inactive work and sampled NBA batches to quiescence, including reactivation from changed values. Positive delays shall preserve future work and checked time arithmetic. Public advances shall preserve signal, fixed-memory, process and event state on execution, capacity, address or budget failures. Future host input deposits shall not affect earlier scheduled events. Pending-event queries shall describe runnable and queued work. Unsupported regions and storage semantics shall remain explicit limitations.
<<<
COMMENT: Bounded implementation acceptance for WP-02, distinct from opaque event-ID transport. Broad timing requirements and full IEEE region conformance are not closed by this slice.
