UID: VS-RTL-INPUT-DEFAULT-001
STATUS: Draft
TITLE: Automatic input default arguments and slot preservation
STATEMENT: >>>
Supported automatic functions and zero-time tasks shall preserve positional and named argument slots, including leading and interior omissions. An omitted input shall require an explicit default and evaluate it only when used in its declaration scope. Missing required inputs, duplicate or unknown names and omitted output targets shall fail closed. Constant-function calls used in elaborated widths shall apply supported constant input defaults before folding. Unsupported constant-default expressions shall be rejected instead of becoming zero. Import shall require matching frontend provenance even when constant calls have folded away.
<<<
